module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.seed_sha256_is_runner_relative

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode, RungRead, FoundOnRung, BelowCeiling }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, MechanicallyPreventable }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

data seed_sha256_is_runner_relative: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "seed_sha256_is_runner_relative" as NonEmptyStr,

  // FOUND AT MITIGATABLE, NOT READ-UNSTATED: the human-readable cause and the interim citation
  // rule are recorded here, and the mitigation is built and MEASURED (the modeled seed-build
  // preamble of gunbc.repo.repo_self_build, consumed by every emitted seed-build step, plus the
  // seed_build_environment axis of gunbc.fleet.fleet_release_bins_key). It is not higher, because
  // the control that would catch a regression is an ON-DEMAND instrument rather than an enrolled
  // gate: the required path does not run the v1 unit tests, so a step that drops a prefix lands
  // green until someone runs the control by hand.
  rung: RungRead {
    found_at: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable },
    standing: BelowCeiling {
      current: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable },
      ceiling: MechanicallyPreventable,
      blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt,
      // Named as a CAPABILITY, not an artifact: an executed check that runs the seed-build
      // reproducibility falsifier (two clones of one commit, each built cold under the preamble
      // authority, asserting equal sha256; and the same pair with the preamble authority disabled,
      // asserting they differ) and fails the seed build on which CI depends, OR the cheaper
      // equivalent -- each emitted seed-build step echoing the preamble's digest into its own
      // receipt, so a step that dropped the authority is visible in the receipt rather than in a
      // hand-run test. Either raises the rung; neither is built yet, which is why this is
      // ClimbableButUnbuilt and not a drop from a held rung.
      trigger_capability: "an executed check on the seed build's own required path that runs the reproducibility falsifier (build twice from two clones of one commit under the preamble authority, assert sha256 equality; rerun with the authority disabled, assert the sha256 differs), or the cheaper floor: every emitted seed-build step echoing the preamble's digest into its receipt so a dropped authority is visible without a hand-run test",
    },
  },

  receipts: [
    "A seed sha256 names a (commit, runner) pair, not a commit, until the seed build pins its path and identity environment: two builds of ONE commit on runners whose absolute checkout path, CARGO_TARGET_DIR, CARGO_HOME, or rustc sysroot differ produce DIFFERENT sha256 values, while one build system with all four pinned is reproducible. Until the seed-build preamble declares the remap prefixes and the tree identity once and every seed-binary build step consumes it, every receipt, verdict, or cache key that cites seed sha256 alone as THE identity of a seed build is falsified by the runner it ran on. The sound interim citation for a seed build is commit + sha256 + host (the runner's identity), never commit + sha256.",

    "MEASURED 2026-10-25 on the ctrl-build runner (linux/amd64, rustc 1.95.0-nightly e943f00), all from commit a430c878e5cfa56f06ce1b461cccac20f415d468, each build cold from a fresh target directory: (1) same checkout path twice, clean tree: IDENTICAL sha256 b8c24b3d — codegen/LTO/cgo contribute no variance on this toolchain. (2) same checkout path plus ONE untracked file: DIFFER (eedf8e3c) — src/v1/stage0/build.rs bakes GUNBC_BUILD_IDENTITY=<git-HEAD> with a '-dirty' suffix whenever git status --porcelain is non-empty, so any runner-local untracked file changes the binary. (3) two independent clones at different absolute paths, both clean: DIFFER (b8c24b3d vs ec03f8ac); objcopy shows the variance lives entirely in .rodata, and strings shows the checkout path baked into the binary (…/g1/src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run/pre_entry_phase.rs in one, …/g2/… in the other) — path literals from the compilation environment with no --remap-path-prefix set anywhere. (4) the fix, measured: two independent clones, each built with RUSTFLAGS='--remap-path-prefix=<its checkout>=/build/checkout --remap-path-prefix=<its target>=/build/target --remap-path-prefix=<its CARGO_HOME>=/build/cargo-home --remap-path-prefix=<its sysroot>=/build/rust' and GUNBC_MATERIALIZED_TREE_IDENTITY pinned to a tree:sha256 value: cmp reports gunbc AND claim_executor byte-IDENTICAL across the two clones. (5) a single runner's own cross-run receipt failure: seed 3dbf6b88 at main a430c878e5cf hashed differently on three runners. Related but distinct: gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.build_cache_key_includes_the_absolute_checkout_path is about the same path inputs poisoning a CACHE KEY; this row is about them poisoning the seed's IDENTITY DIGEST.",

    "THE CENSUS THE REPAIR MUST COVER (the seed's own build steps, by producer; a step outside this list silently gets a runner-relative sha256): every seed-binary build step composes its `run:` text through gunbc.repo.repo_self_build repo_self_seed_build_step_run, which puts the modeled preamble of repo_self_build_env_stmts FIRST so the refusal guards abort before cargo starts. Producers today: dag/gunbc/fleet/fleet_converge_workflow.dag (three sites -- fleet_converge_plan_revision_pair_build_step, fleet_converge_in_job_compiler_pair_build_step, fleet_converge_hosted_gunbc_build_step) and dag/gunbc/fleet/fleet_workflow_steps.dag (the two release-bins steps); plus the floor-wrapped path, gunbc.witness.witness_floor_workflow witness_floor_build_step, which composes the same preamble OUTSIDE its receipt wrapper so the floor log stays clean, and carries the jobs heal, heal-publish, drift-watch, instrument-dispatch, branch-run-grant-broker, compiler-gate and witnesses; plus the cache-key axis gunbc.fleet.fleet_release_bins_key release_bins_seed_build_environment_digest, which needs the digest because that job SKIPS the build on a cache hit and would otherwise key a build it never ran. A new seed-build step joins the census by calling the one wrapper, not by spelling cargo.",

    "WHAT IS AND IS NOT REPRODUCIBLE UPSTREAM OF THE COMPILER (measured 2026-10-26, same runner, same commit): the generated .rs inputs do NOT vary. Two INDEPENDENT clones of one commit, one --regen-round-cost pass in each, .git stripped, diff -r over the two trees: EMPTY, aggregate whole-tree sha256 equal. So the variance this row is about is compile-grain (path bake plus the build identity), a receipt-grain bug -- not a non-deterministic generator, which would have been a correctness bug and outranked it, and not toolchain-level, which would have needed an operator decision. The shape of the probe matters: re-running regen twice in ONE clone and reporting a difference is not evidence, because the second pass sees a different working state; the two-clone form is the only honest one.",

    "SCOPE OF THE CLAIM: the second axis is the build identity, not the paths. A producer that leaves GUNBC_MATERIALIZED_TREE_IDENTITY unset makes build.rs fall back to git HEAD plus the dirty flag, so the same commit builds different bytes on a dirty runner. A producer that pins the tree identity but not the remap prefixes still gets path-dependent bytes. BOTH must be declared for one commit to give one sha256, which is what the seed-build preamble (remap prefixes + tree identity, declared once in the .dag and consumed by every emitted seed-build step) exists to guarantee. THE MITIGATION NOW SHIPS: the preamble authority is declared once in the .dag, consumed by every emitted seed-build step, and keyed into the release-bins axis. ITS CONTROL IS A HAND-RUN CARGO TEST, not a gunbc test label -- there is deliberately no row for it in gunbc.instrument_targets, and claiming a label here would name an instrument that cannot be run as named. Name of the control: the #[ignore]d test seed_build_reproducibility_falsifier in src/v1/stage0/src/compiler_tests.rs (authored in src/v1/compiler_tests_rust.dag), re-derived by running `cargo test --lib -p v1-compiler -- --ignored --nocapture --test-threads=1 seed_build_reproducibility_falsifier`. IT PRINTS ITS OWN TWO ARMS; this row deliberately does not copy them: the green arm builds two independent clones of one commit through the preamble authority and requires ONE sha256, the red arm builds the same commit with the preamble authority disabled and requires a DIFFERENT sha256 -- and it refuses before building if the committed seed-build steps do not carry every pair of repo_self_seed_build_remaps. Its status is #[ignore]d and hand-run: the required path does not run the v1 unit tests (DESIGN, Building and checks), so nothing executes it on a pull request. That is why the rung the executed evidence establishes is mitigatable and not higher, and why the trigger capability above is named as the thing that would raise it."
  ],

  evidence: []
}
